Other files which are needed for this example are the same as in the
"Eirene_bench_difft_physics" run: eirene*.out, geometry_*.inp, 
ue_rect_slab.geom, uedata_rect_slab.u. Note that ratecalc must be used to
generate the netCDF files for hchexold (hchex.nc).  In hchex.nc, the
value of sgvmax is left at its default value of 0.0 to effectively disable
rejection, as is done in the EIRENE run. The file hionize.nc required
manually alterations following generation by ratecalc in order for it to
work as required. Hence, the binary file is included here.
It should be regenerated if the format (xsection.hweb) of the data changes.

Because this geometry differs from the normal single-null configuration
expected by readgeometry and readbackground, specific internal changes
were required to those codes. Before compiling readgeometry and 
readbackground, the flag GEOMETRY must be changed from GENERAL
to UEDGE_RECT_SLAB to enable these changes. Be sure to reset those flags to 
GENERAL prior to running the code with other geometries.

This example will now also serve as a performance benchmark. However, some
aspects of this benchmark are not yet standard parts of the code (principally
because they result in increases in variance) and must also be
enabled by compiler switches:
 * geomint.hweb - PLANE_SURFACES 1 (normal is "0"; with "1", the code drops
   the quadratic terms in the surface representation).
 * tallysetup.web - OPTIMIZE 1 (this defines a minimal set of tallies, 4
   as compared to the 14 or so obtained with the default "0").
 * collide.web - RR 1 (does Russian roulette when molecular dissociation
   products are both the same test species; with "0", both such products
   would be tracked).

The text and primary netCDF output here are for 80,000 flights. The run
time on a Sun UltraSPARC 2 running SunOS 5.5.1 and V. 4.2 of f77 with
"-O4" optimization is 626 seconds (via the shell command "time flighttest").

The results from a 4000 flight run are included here as well in 
degas2_4000_out.nc.




A reduced set of tallies, 
obtained by changing the flag OPTIMIZE from "0" to "1" in tallysetup, is 
used for these output data. 80000 flights were run. A second run with 
just 4000 flights is in degas2_4000_out.nc
